{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-06T22:58:09.487Z","data":{"text":"Task complete. Summary of what was done:\n\n**Implemented**\n- `src/core/status/watcher-line.ts` (new): `formatWatcherLine(state)` renders the \"Watcher line\" table — background/restarting/terminal/not-running rows with the `, waiting: <reason>` suffix — from the `WatchState` that `readWatchState` returns.\n- `src/cli/inbox.ts`: text output is now `formatInboxText(inbox)` + newline + watcher line from `readWatchState(cwd, options.home)`; `--json` output unchanged; nothing writes a watch record.\n- `src/cli/status.ts`: `statusCommand` takes an optional `home`, prints overview, an empty line, the watcher line, and `Log: <path>` when `watch.log` exists.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/watcher-line.test.ts` (new): covers every \"Watcher line\" scenario, every table row, the waiting suffix, \"Entirely empty inbox\" on `formatInboxText`, and command cases running `inboxCommand`/`statusCommand` against a temporary home with records written for `process.pid` (including `--json` key contract, the `Log:` line, and that neither command writes a record).\n- `tests/inbox.test.ts`: the two bare-`osq` cases now expect `Watcher: not running — osq watch --background` after the inbox text; nothing else changed.\n\n**Verification**\n- Task verify (`node --import tsx --import ./tests/git-test-env.ts --test tests/watcher-line.test.ts tests/inbox.test.ts`): 29/29 pass.\n- Proposal verify (`pnpm verify`): completed green through typecheck, build, the full test suite, and lint.\n- Result file written to `openspec/changes/155-watch-service/.run/results/5.md`."}}
